Key lesson
- “No deopt hits” does not imply no interpreter overhead: strict-force internals can still silently bypass compiled dispatch.

Outstanding bottlenecks after this fix
- `mat_mul` remains dominated by size-2 + explicit `DUP_CELL`; this path likely needs DUP-cell pressure reduction and/or stricter expression-level lowering for its hot loops.
- Some residual captures (`EXPR_APP_ARG_CAPTURE`, `EXPR_CTR_FIELD_CAPTURE`) still appear in select canaries but are low count.

Next steps
1) Add lightweight heap kind attribution (APP vs OP2 vs DP vs CTR site families) to avoid blind size-2 optimization.
2) Revisit non-self recursion architecture (SCC/trampoline) once hot strict paths are compiled.
3) Expand strict lowering only where WNF semantics guarantee demand, keeping lazy contexts unchanged.
